For those that have some patches accepted, it would be good to start 
working on your application, if you have not done so already.  The link to 
the application is here:

https://outreachy.gnome.org/?q=program_home&prg=5

There is some information about the structure of the application here:

https://wiki.gnome.org/Outreachy#Submit_an_Application
https://wiki.gnome.org/Outreachy#Application_Form

Please follow the additional instructions for the Linux kernel here:

http://kernelnewbies.org/OutreachyApply

One important part of the application is the timeline for the project.  
You may need to interact with your potential mentor to put this together.

Finally, if you have submitted a good number of patches, even if they are 
not all yet accepted, it would be good to be contacting mentors and 
starting on the specific small tasks, for the projects that interest you.

julia

